From 1c41b9c6988584ed2622693099ecbe1b21344e00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 19:33:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11336/11362] fix(arc): require each tool's arguments in the
 induction grammar

The REQ-7044 grammar constrained the envelope only. `arguments` was any
JSON object, so `{"name":"run_engine_on_transitions","arguments":{}}`
was grammatical. The recorded 0.8B trial returned that envelope twice
(31 tokens, 11.29 s, no engine) and counted both as parsed calls.
llama.cpp's own test-gbnf-validator (build b9606) confirms the
acceptance with no model. A grammar that admits an empty shell makes
every model result on the transport uninterpretable, so this fix comes
before any 27B trial.

What changed:
- `_tool_grammar` takes the session schemas. Each tool gets its own
  arguments rule: required keys first, in schema order, with their JSON
  type. Required strings are non-empty. Enums are literals. Optional
  keys may follow. A tool with no required keys accepts any object.
- `_lift_grammar_response` rejects an envelope that lacks a required
  argument or sends it empty: no dispatch, not counted as parsed.
- The grammar text is built once per session from a deep copy of the
  frozen schemas. A first draft rebuilt it per turn from the live dicts,
  and the frozen-names test caught a mutated candidate name leaking
  into the second request.
- The grammar prompt no longer shows an empty arguments example.
- `python/carnot/testing/gbnf_match.py`: a model-free GBNF reader for
  the subset these grammars use. `tests/python/test_gbnf_match.py` pins
  it to test-gbnf-validator verdicts on 18 cases for the old grammar
  (sha256 6a09d16d..., 614 bytes) and the new one. 36 of 36 agree.
- Spec: REQ-ARC-WMTE-7046, two scenarios. REQ-7044 gets an amendment.

Instrument audit: the first proof run reported the full call INVALID
because json.dumps default spacing violates the whitespace-rigid root
rule. That was the instrument, not the grammar. Kept as case P.

Verified: 164 focused tests pass (grammar transport, tool loop, repair,
persistence, reader). ruff and mypy clean on the changed files.

Not yet done: mutation proofs at the call sites and the 27B trial on
GPU 1. Both follow in later commits on this branch.

